# Copy to .env.local to override. Every VITE_ variable this app reads is listed here — a var that is
# not in this file is a var nobody knows exists, and all of them are read at BUILD time (Vite inlines
# them), so a change means a rebuild, never a restart of something.

# ── The registry, the relay and the rooms ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The Phase 3 backend: registration, claim, inbox, push, and the transfer rooms of §7.1
# (moltworker `worker/src/infinite/`, behind INFINITE_ENABLED — §9.4). Unset it and src/transfer's
# config falls back to an unroutable `.invalid` placeholder, which is what makes the UI say "not
# connected yet" instead of spinning; see roomsConfigured() in src/transfer/config.ts.
#VITE_INFINITE_API_BASE=https://<the worker origin>/infinite

# The 00 relay — where this browser reaches your Mac's engine, and where your phone reaches this
# browser (§8.4, §8.5). The DEFAULT is already the real one and is derived from the engine: the
# origin of apps/00d/src/overblast-client.ts's DEFAULT_BASE (https://brain.deployd.network/v1), which
# is exactly what apps/00d/src/mobile-connect-client.ts's relayFor() talks to — `/api/engines/…` sits
# at the worker root, not under /v1. Set this only to point at a local or staging worker; `off`, an
# empty-ish value or a `.invalid` host makes the Mac card say "not connected yet" (relayConfigured()
# in src/mac/config.ts) rather than failing as a bare network error.
#VITE_RELAY_ORIGIN=https://brain.deployd.network

# The Web Push key this browser subscribes against (§5.7). ONLY a fallback: the app card's
# `push.vapidPublicKey` wins when the registry publishes one, because a subscription minted against
# the wrong registry's key can never be sent to. Public half only — the private half lives in the
# worker's secrets and nowhere near a build.
#VITE_INFINITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ── The local brain (§12.7) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the LiteRT (MediaPipe) Gemma weights are served from: the code defaults to the public mirror
# on R2 (https://dl.0-0.chat/litert, decided 2026-09-10, docs/HANDOFF-infinite-agent.md §12.7,
# published by scripts/publish-litert-models.sh). Set another host, or `off` to run WebLLM only (the
# app then says so on the Connections screen).
#VITE_LITERT_MODEL_BASE=https://dl.0-0.chat/litert

# MediaPipe's wasm runtime. Left EMPTY on purpose: dev and self-hosted builds serve it from their own
# origin (vite.config.ts copies it), which is what keeps the local brain offline-capable. The hosted
# site sets it in its own .env.local to https://dl.0-0.chat/mediapipe/genai/0.10.29/wasm because
# Cloudflare's asset layer cannot carry a 27 MB file.
VITE_LITERT_WASM_BASE=

# ── The live preview (docs/HANDOFF-infinite-agent.md review item 15) ─────────────────────────────

# The origin of the preview host — apps/infinite-preview-site, a Worker that holds no data and exists
# only to BE A DIFFERENT ORIGIN. Measured: on one origin a browser gives a frame either an opaque
# identity (never served by a service worker) or ours (served, and holding the vault), so a live,
# navigable preview needs a second origin and the pane falls back to a snapshot without one. The code
# default is the workers.dev link the integrator deploys to; `off`, an empty value or a `.invalid`
# host makes the pane say so and stay on the snapshot road rather than framing nothing.
#VITE_PREVIEW_ORIGIN=https://infinite-preview.powerhouse.workers.dev
